This product includes data derived from third-party Apache-2.0 projects:

  server/src/matter/clusters.json
    Cluster, command, attribute and event identifiers, the TLV context tags of
    each command's request and response, and the payload field types, extracted
    from the cluster definitions generated by rs-matter.
      rs-matter — https://github.com/project-chip/rs-matter
      Copyright the Project CHIP Authors, Apache-2.0
    Regenerate with tools/build_registry.py; see that file for the procedure.

  server/src/api/vendors.json
    The Matter vendor-id to vendor-name table, extracted from
    packages/ws-controller/src/data/VendorIDs.ts.
      matterjs-server — https://github.com/matter-js/matterjs-server
      Copyright 2025-2026 Open Home Foundation, Apache-2.0

  server/src/matter/wire_naming.rs
    The acronym list and field-name overrides are a port of
    packages/ws-client/src/wire-naming.ts from matterjs-server (as above).
    Clients index command payloads by these names, so the transform has to
    agree with the reference exactly.

The WebSocket protocol this server implements is defined by matterjs-server.
This is an independent implementation of that wire contract; it shares no code
with it beyond the data and naming rules listed above.
